  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDU: Leadership for Change in Education (Teach for LAC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Latin America and Caribbean Regional):  This activity is working to improve teacher quality and teacher support resources in low-income and hard-to-staff communities of select countries in the LAC region. The purpose of the activity is to develop collective leadership to improve education quality. With FY 2022 funds, and after an approved extension (requested in Fall 2022), the activity will continue supporting teacher leadership programs through local partners in Colombia, Ecuador, and Paraguay, and the activity will support the establishment of a new teacher leadership program through a local partner in Guatemala. Key interventions and outcomes will include the end line student learning assessments, recruitment and training of new leaders in the teaching profession, family and community engagement, the expansion of education services to additional regions in each country, and alumni network engagement across leadership pathways. Furthermore, given this activity&apos;s focus on improving quality education, including for girls, we expect the activity to improve school access and retention rates for girls, which has been proven to reduce child early marriage. This activity supports the WHA-LAC Joint Regional Strategy objective of strengthened health and education system and improved inclusive access by improving the quality of teaching in hard-to-staff and difficult-to-reach schools/communities, which improves access for under-served students, as well as supporting alumni of the teacher leadership programs to become leaders in the education sector over the course of their careers. ..</narrative>
  </description>
